\section{Dataset}
\label{sec:data}

In our experiments we have used the first 2 years of the \emph{Telegraph} dataset that includes 812,975 news articles~\cite{baird_sequence_2017}.
The training set contains 813,062 articles with each article containing between 4 and 1000 sentences, with the average article length being 30.3 sentences.
The test set contains 9,822 articles with each article containing between 5 and 100 sentences, with the average article length being 25.5 sentences.
